attack:T1169
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Sudo"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "The sudoers file, /etc/sudoers, describes which users can run which commands and from which terminals. This also describes which commands users can run as other users or groups. This provides the idea of least privilege such that users are running in their lowest possible permissions for most of the time and only elevate to other users or permissions as needed, typically by prompting for a password. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1548.003."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1169" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0004 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1548.003 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1169> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1170
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Mshta"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Mshta.exe is a utility that executes Microsoft HTML Applications (HTA). HTA files have the file extension .hta. HTAs are standalone applications that execute using the same models and technologies of Internet Explorer, but outside of the browser. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1218.005."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1170" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0005 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0002 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1218.005 ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-04-14"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1170> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1171
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "LLMNR/NBT-NS Poisoning and Relay"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Link-Local Multicast Name Resolution (LLMNR) and NetBIOS Name Service (NBT-NS) are Microsoft Windows components that serve as alternate methods of host identification. LLMNR is based upon the Domain Name System (DNS) format and allows hosts on the same local link to perform name resolution for other hosts. NBT-NS identifies systems on a local network by their NetBIOS name. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1557.001."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1171" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0006 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1557.001 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1171> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1172
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Domain Fronting"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Domain fronting takes advantage of routing schemes in Content Delivery Networks (CDNs) and other services which host multiple domains to obfuscate the intended destination of HTTPS traffic or traffic tunneled through HTTPS. The technique involves using different domain names in the SNI field of the TLS header and the Host field of the HTTP header. If both domains are served from the same CDN, then the CDN may route to the address specified in the HTTP header after unwrapping the TLS header. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1090.004."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1172" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0011 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1090.004 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1172> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1173
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Dynamic Data Exchange"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Windows Dynamic Data Exchange (DDE) is a client-server protocol for one-time and/or continuous inter-process communication (IPC) between applications. Once a link is established, applications can autonomously exchange transactions consisting of strings, warm data links (notifications when a data item changes), hot data links (duplications of changes to a data item), and requests for command execution. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1559.002."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1173" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0002 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1559.002 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1173> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1174
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Password Filter DLL"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Windows password filters are password policy enforcement mechanisms for both domain and local accounts. Filters are implemented as dynamic link libraries (DLLs) containing a method to validate potential passwords against password policies. Filter DLLs can be positioned on local computers for local accounts and/or domain controllers for domain accounts. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1556.002."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1174" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0006 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1556.002 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1174> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1175
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Component Object Model and Distributed COM"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "**This technique has been deprecated. Please use Distributed Component Object Model and Component Object Model.** Deprecated by MITRE ATT&CK."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1175" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0008 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0002 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1175> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1176
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Software Extensions"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Adversaries may abuse software extensions to establish persistent access to victim systems. Software extensions are modular components that enhance or customize the functionality of software applications, including web browsers, Integrated Development Environments (IDEs), and other platforms. Extensions are typically installed via official marketplaces, app stores, or manually loaded by users, and they often inherit the permissions and access levels of the host application."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1176" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1176> ;
	.

attack:T1176.001
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf attack:T1176 ;
	rdfs:label "Software Extensions: Browser Extensions"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Adversaries may abuse internet browser extensions to establish persistent access to victim systems. Browser extensions or plugins are small programs that can add functionality to and customize aspects of internet browsers. They can be installed directly via a local file or custom URL or through a browser's app store - an official online platform where users can browse, install, and manage extensions for a specific web browser."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1176.001" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-09-22"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1176/001> ;
	.

attack:T1176.002
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf attack:T1176 ;
	rdfs:label "Software Extensions: IDE Extensions"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Adversaries may abuse an integrated development environment (IDE) extension to establish persistent access to victim systems. IDEs such as Visual Studio Code, IntelliJ IDEA, and Eclipse support extensions - software components that add features like code linting, auto-completion, task automation, or integration with tools like Git and Docker."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1176.002" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-04-23"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1176/002> ;
	.

attack:T1177
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "LSASS Driver"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "The Windows security subsystem is a set of components that manage and enforce the security policy for a computer or domain. The Local Security Authority (LSA) is the main component responsible for local security policy and user authentication. The LSA includes multiple dynamic link libraries (DLLs) associated with various other security functions, all of which run in the context of the LSA Subsystem Service (LSASS) lsass.exe process. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1547.008."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1177" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0002 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1547.008 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1177> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1178
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "SID-History Injection"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "The Windows security identifier (SID) is a unique value that identifies a user or group account. SIDs are used by Windows security in both security descriptors and access tokens. An account can hold additional SIDs in the SID-History Active Directory attribute, allowing inter-operable account migration between domains (e.g., all values in SID-History are included in access tokens). Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1134.005."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1178" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0004 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1134.005 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1178> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1179
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Hooking"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Windows processes often leverage application programming interface (API) functions to perform tasks that require reusable system resources. Windows API functions are typically stored in dynamic-link libraries (DLLs) as exported functions. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1056.004."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1179" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0004 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0006 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1056.004 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1179> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1180
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Screensaver"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Screensavers are programs that execute after a configurable time of user inactivity and consist of Portable Executable (PE) files with a .scr file extension. The Windows screensaver application scrnsave.scr is located in C:\\Windows\\System32\\, and C:\\Windows\\sysWOW64\\ on 64-bit Windows systems, along with screensavers included with base Windows installations. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1546.002."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1180" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1546.002 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1180> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1181
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Extra Window Memory Injection"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Before creating a window, graphical Windows-based processes must prescribe to or register a windows class, which stipulate appearance and behavior (via windows procedures, which are functions that handle input/output of data). Registration of new windows classes can include a request for up to 40 bytes of extra window memory (EWM) to be appended to the allocated memory of each instance of that class. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1055.011."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1181" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0005 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0004 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1055.011 ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-04-14"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1181> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1182
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "AppCert DLLs"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Dynamic-link libraries (DLLs) that are specified in the AppCertDLLs Registry key under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager are loaded into every process that calls the ubiquitously used application programming interface (API) functions CreateProcess, CreateProcessAsUser, CreateProcessWithLoginW, CreateProcessWithTokenW, or WinExec. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1546.009."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1182" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0004 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1546.009 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1182> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1183
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Image File Execution Options Injection"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Image File Execution Options (IFEO) enable a developer to attach a debugger to an application. When a process is created, a debugger present in an application’s IFEO will be prepended to the application’s name, effectively launching the new process under the debugger (e.g., “C:\\dbg\\ntsd.exe -g notepad.exe”). Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1546.012."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1183" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0004 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0003 ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0005 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1546.012 ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-04-14"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1183> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1184
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "SSH Hijacking"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Secure Shell (SSH) is a standard means of remote access on Linux and macOS systems. It allows a user to connect to another system via an encrypted tunnel, commonly authenticating through a password, certificate or the use of an asymmetric encryption key pair. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1563.001."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1184" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0008 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1563.001 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1184> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1185
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Browser Session Hijacking"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Adversaries may take advantage of security vulnerabilities and inherent functionality in browser software to change content, modify user-behaviors, and intercept information as part of various browser session hijacking techniques."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1185" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0009 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-05-12"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1185> ;
	.

attack:T1186
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Process Doppelgänging"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Windows Transactional NTFS (TxF) was introduced in Vista as a method to perform safe file operations. To ensure data integrity, TxF enables only one transacted handle to write to a file at a given time. Until the write handle transaction is terminated, all other handles are isolated from the writer and may only read the committed version of the file that existed at the time the handle was opened. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1055.013."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1186" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0005 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1055.013 ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-04-14"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1186> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1187
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Forced Authentication"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Adversaries may gather credential material by invoking or forcing a user to automatically provide authentication information through a mechanism in which they can intercept."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1187" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0006 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1187> ;
	.

attack:T1188
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Multi-hop Proxy"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "To disguise the source of malicious traffic, adversaries may chain together multiple proxies. Typically, a defender will be able to identify the last proxy traffic traversed before it enters their network; the defender may or may not be able to identify any previous proxies before the last-hop proxy. This technique makes identifying the original source of the malicious traffic even more difficult by requiring the defender to trace malicious traffic through several proxies to identify its source. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1090.003."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1188" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0011 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Linux" ;
	dcterms:coverage "Windows" ;
	dcterms:coverage "macOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/enterprise/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1090.003 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1188> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

