attack:T1463
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Manipulate Device Communication"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "If network traffic between the mobile device and a remote server is not securely protected, then an attacker positioned on the network may be able to manipulate network communication without being detected. For example, FireEye researchers found in 2014 that 68% of the top 1,000 free applications in the Google Play Store had at least one Transport Layer Security (TLS) implementation vulnerability potentially opening the applications' network traffic to adversary-in-the-middle attacks. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1638."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1463" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0038 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1638 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1463> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1464
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Network Denial of Service"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Adversaries may perform Network Denial of Service (DoS) attacks to degrade or block the availability of targeted resources to users. Network DoS can be performed by exhausting the network bandwidth that services rely on, or by jamming the signal going to or coming from devices."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1464" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0034 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-05-19"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1464> ;
	.

attack:T1465
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Rogue Wi-Fi Access Points"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary could set up unauthorized Wi-Fi access points or compromise existing access points and, if the device connects to them, carry out network-based attacks such as eavesdropping on or modifying network communication. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1638."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1465" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0038 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1638 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1465> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1466
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Downgrade to Insecure Protocols"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary could cause the mobile device to use less secure protocols, for example by jamming frequencies used by newer protocols such as LTE and only allowing older protocols such as GSM to communicate. Use of less secure protocols may make communication easier to eavesdrop upon or manipulate. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1638."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1466" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0038 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1638 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1466> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1467
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Rogue Cellular Base Station"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary could set up a rogue cellular base station and then use it to eavesdrop on or manipulate cellular device communication. A compromised cellular femtocell could be used to carry out this technique. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1638."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1467" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0038 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1638 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1467> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1468
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Remotely Track Device Without Authorization"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary who is able to obtain unauthorized access to or misuse authorized access to cloud services (e.g. Google's Android Device Manager or Apple iCloud's Find my iPhone) or to an enterprise mobility management (EMM) / mobile device management (MDM) server console could use that access to track mobile devices. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1430.001."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1468" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0039 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1430.001 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1468> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1469
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Remotely Wipe Data Without Authorization"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary who is able to obtain unauthorized access to or misuse authorized access to cloud services (e.g. Google's Android Device Manager or Apple iCloud's Find my iPhone) or to an EMM console could use that access to wipe enrolled devices. Deprecated by MITRE ATT&CK."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1469" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0039 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1469> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1470
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Obtain Device Cloud Backups"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary who is able to obtain unauthorized access to or misuse authorized access to cloud backup services (e.g. Google's Android backup service or Apple's iCloud) could use that access to obtain sensitive data stored in device backups. For example, the Elcomsoft Phone Breaker product advertises the ability to retrieve iOS backup data from Apple's iCloud. Elcomsoft also describes obtaining WhatsApp communication histories from backups stored in iCloud. Deprecated by MITRE ATT&CK."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1470" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0039 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1470> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1471
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Data Encrypted for Impact"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary may encrypt files stored on a mobile device to prevent the user from accessing them. This may be done in order to extract monetary compensation from a victim in exchange for decryption or a decryption key (ransomware) or to render data permanently inaccessible in cases where the key is not saved or transmitted."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1471" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0034 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1471> ;
	.

attack:T1472
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Generate Fraudulent Advertising Revenue"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An adversary could seek to generate fraudulent advertising revenue from mobile devices, for example by triggering automatic clicks of advertising links without user involvement. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1643."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1472" ;
	dcterms:subject attack-tactic:TA0034 ;
	dcterms:coverage "Android" ;
	dcterms:coverage "iOS" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
	dcterms:isReplacedBy attack:T1643 ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1472> ;
	owl:deprecated true ;
	.

attack:T1473
	a
		owl:Class ,
		action:Technique
		;
	rdfs:subClassOf action:Action ;
	rdfs:label "Malicious or Vulnerable Built-in Device Functionality"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "MITRE ATT&CK technique T1473. Revoked by MITRE ATT&CK; superseded by T1474."@en ;
	action:techniqueID "T1473" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf <https://attack.mitre.org/matrices/mobile/> ;
